{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>As for Me, behold, My covenant is with you.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote, by way of truth: the sense of הנה בריתי אתך is like the sense of ״והנה אנכי עמך״ (Exodus 3:12), ״כי אהיה עמך״ (1 Kings 8:57 — ״יהי ה׳ אלהינו עמנו״). That is to say, the covenant will be with him, and therefore he will be fruitful and multiply; and afterward He commanded that Abraham keep this covenant, and that circumcision be the sign of the covenant. And behold, this sign is the sign of the Sabbath, and therefore he would push it off — and understand this — end of his words, of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The citation כי אהיה עמך does not match 1 Kings 8:57 as Rabbeinu Bahya's prooftext line suggests; the Ramban's comment appears to join Exodus 3:12 and 1 Kings 8:57 as parallel prooftexts; the text as written is translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:49.714340502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}